const GRASS_REQ = `GRASS LIVELINESS + GENTLE SWAY ADD-ON (user request 2026-10-04, explicit OK: "i want the gentle sway of the plants with the wind, and do 1 and 4"). The ground reads as a carpet at the phone camera; make the grass physically present and lively, and let the plants move gently with the game's wind. IN SCOPE: real tuft MESHES, the ground textures, and a vertex-sway shader for PLANTS ONLY driven by the game's Wind (Unity/Assets/Scripts/Course/Wind.cs: one speed 0-20 mph and one direction per hole, DirectionDegrees = where it blows toward, degrees right of +D = down the hole; GolfGame.Wind is set when a hole starts; the HUD arrow already shows it). STILL OUT OF SCOPE: grass cards, a runtime near-camera grass ring, any motion on the ground, rocks, masonry, water, lava, surf, waterfall or sky (lava and everything else stay STATIC), editing tennis files / TennisWater / QualitySettings.
(1) EDGE FRINGE: tuft meshes (<= 120 faces; the dense ones cheaper) standing taller and denser along the rough edge of the fairway / green / pad rims, the path edges (Needle), shore tops and cliff lips, with varied lean (+-12 degrees), height (0.6-1.8x of the library tuft) and clump grouping (clusters of 3-7 plus a few singles, not a grid). Never on Fairway/Green/Bunker/Tee outlines, never on water, never inside a 4 m radius of any shot ball position in the stills configs (1.5 m around the tee ball), never hiding the pin or flag (>= 6 m clear), tuft tops <= 0.55 yd above ground near the ball corridor, never under the ball.
(2) MOW-BAND LIFE: Fairway_C / Green_C get stronger band contrast (about +-12% luminance) and per-band sheen (band-specific smoothness through the albedo alpha channel with URP _SMOOTHNESS_TEXTURE_ALBEDO_CHANNEL_A enabled by GolfLook, or an equally cheap texture-side equivalent) plus blade-lean streaks in the normal map; hue stays 64-73 under the golf key light, no clipping, no post.
(3) GENTLE SWAY: every PLANT_* library mesh carries sway data as a vertex colour attribute exported through postcard_look_lib.export_look_fbx(colors_type): R = sway weight 0..1 (0 at the root/pinned point rising to 1 at the free tip; tufts/flowers/agave by height, shrubs low, vines pinned at the attach point and swinging toward the bottom), G = per-vertex phase 0..1, B = 0, A = 1. A new golf-owned URP shader GolfArcade/GolfPlants (Unity/Assets/Resources/Course/Shaders/GolfPlants.shader) is the ONLY shader allowed to read time: it displaces vertices in WORLD space along the wind direction (plus a small crosswise component) by weight x amplitude x a sum of two slow sines (about 0.35-0.9 Hz) with a per-instance phase hashed from the world XZ position, so no two clumps move together; amplitude scales with wind speed (a faint idle breeze at 0 mph, about 25% of full), gust variation, hard caps: tuft tip <= 0.06 yd, flower <= 0.05, shrub <= 0.03, vine <= 0.08 at 20 mph; no popping, no stretching of the base. It keeps the shared LK_PLANTS palette atlas, GPU instancing and SRP Batcher compatibility, receives lighting and shadows like URP Lit (ForwardLit with main + additional lights + SH ambient + fog, ShadowCaster and DepthOnly passes that apply the SAME sway) and compiles for iOS/Metal. A small golf-only driver (GolfWindSway, Unity/Assets/Scripts/Course/) sets global shader values every frame (_GolfWind: xyz = wind direction x amplitude, w = time; a static FreezeTime override for deterministic stills) from GolfGame.Wind; GolfGame.cs gets the minimal hook where Wind is assigned. GolfLook maps LK_PLANTS to the new shader (same texture, same tint, same smoothness).
(4) BUDGETS: <= 250k visible triangles per hole (Split was at 238k: the fringe must be paid for by cheaper tuft variants or by trimming low-value props, measured, never above 250k), FBX <= 20 MB, no animation clips, no grass cards.
GATE LINES to report: GRASS_FRINGE_PRESENT (counts, heights, coverage along rough edges), GRASS_NOT_ON_PLAY_SURFACES, GRASS_NOT_ON_WATER, GRASS_BALL_CLEAR, GRASS_TRI_BUDGET, GRASS_STILL_ALIVE (Game-view stills: lower-60% luminance sd and the share of the frame with visible tuft silhouettes vs the round-1 stills + a skeptic vision verdict: does the near ground read as living grass, not a carpet), PLANT_SWAY_COLORS (every PLANT_* mesh in blend AND FBX re-import has the colour attribute, root weight ~0, tip weight > .6; mutants without it FAIL), SWAY_SHADER_COMPILES (Unity compile + shader has no errors, Metal-compatible constructs), SWAY_ONLY_PLANTS (the word _Time / Time.time driving visuals appears only in GolfPlants.shader and the driver; lava/surf/fall/ground/rocks/water pixels identical between two frames 1.2 s apart), SWAY_GENTLE (measured max vertex displacement per plant kind vs the caps, at 0 / 10 / 20 mph), SWAY_WIND_DRIVEN (direction follows Wind.DirectionDegrees in world X/Z, amplitude monotonic with speed, idle breeze small but non-zero), SWAY_STILLS_DETERMINISTIC (two stills at the same frozen time are pixel-identical), SWAY_FRAME_PAIR (two stills of each hole 1.2 s apart with a fixed 12 mph wind differ at plant pixels only, by more than noise and within the caps), plus all earlier gates unchanged (grass hue 64-73, ball and flag visible, no flat colour, scoring identical, hole 7 byte-identical, tennis files untouched).`

